---
title: Creating a Payment Gateway
description: Integrate payment providers into FOSSBilling.
---

This guide walks you through building a payment gateway adapter to integrate providers like Stripe, PayPal, or any payment processor into FOSSBilling.

## How Payment Gateways Work

1. **Payment Initiation** — Client clicks "Pay", FOSSBilling calls `getHtml()` to display the payment form
2. **Payment Processing** — Gateway processes the payment
3. **Verification** — Gateway calls `ipn.php`, which triggers `processTransaction()` to verify and record the payment

## Getting Started

### File Location

Place your adapter in:

{% filetree %}
- library/Payment/Adapter/
  - MyGateway.php              # Single file
  - MyGateway/
    - MyGateway.php          # Or subdirectory for complex gateways
{% /filetree %}

### Naming

- **File:** `MyGateway.php` (PascalCase)
- **Class:** `Payment_Adapter_MyGateway`

## Stripe one-time payment walkthrough

The [bundled Stripe adapter in FOSSBilling 0.8.9](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Payment/Adapter/Stripe.php) shows how a one-time invoice payment moves from checkout to crediting the client.

1. **Create the payment from the invoice.** `getConfig()` declares the gateway settings and supported payment types. `getHtml()` loads the invoice, then `_generateForm()` creates a Stripe PaymentIntent using the invoice total in minor units and its currency. It records the invoice, client, and gateway IDs as metadata. An idempotency key based on the invoice, gateway, and checkout parameters lets Stripe reuse the intent on a retried create request. [Checkout code](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Payment/Adapter/Stripe.php#L1750-L1770)
2. **Verify the provider response.** For a webhook, `processWebhookEvent()` verifies the `Stripe-Signature` header against the raw request body with the test or live signing secret. It checks that the event belongs to this gateway before dispatching it. For a browser callback, the adapter retrieves the PaymentIntent from Stripe and checks the gateway ID and, for a linked invoice, the invoice ID and currency. [Webhook verification](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Payment/Adapter/Stripe.php#L639-L706) · [Browser callback verification](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Payment/Adapter/Stripe.php#L346-L377)
3. **Validate the amount before crediting funds.** Both paths require a succeeded PaymentIntent and convert the amount from Stripe's minor units. For a linked invoice, they pass the amount and the invoice total with tax to `validatePaymentAmount()`. The helper rejects underpayments beyond its rounding tolerance and logs significant overpayments. [Payment application](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Payment/Adapter/Stripe.php#L1298-L1339) · [Amount validation](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/modules/Invoice/Service.php#L1127-L1143)
4. **Serialise callbacks for the same payment.** The browser callback and webhook use the same database lock keyed by gateway and PaymentIntent ID. While holding it, the adapter checks for an existing transaction for the payment, skips an already-paid invoice, and uses `claimForProcessing()` to atomically claim the transaction row before crediting funds. [Payment lock and duplicate check](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/library/Payment/Adapter/Stripe.php#L1022-L1123) · [Transaction claim](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/blob/0.8.9/src/modules/Invoice/ServiceTransaction.php#L475-L505)

Validate the payment's gateway, invoice, currency, and amount on every path your adapter uses to apply a credit. Record processing errors on the transaction so they can be reviewed in the admin panel.

## Configuration Options

FOSSBilling injects these into `$this->config`:

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `notify_url` | IPN/webhook callback URL |
| `return_url` | Browser return through `/invoice/payment-return` with status `ok` |
| `cancel_url` | Browser return through `/invoice/payment-return` with status `cancel` |
| `thankyou_url` | Browser return through `/invoice/payment-return` with status `thankyou` |
| `test_mode` | Whether in sandbox mode |

## Browser Returns

Use the injected `return_url`, `cancel_url`, and `thankyou_url` unchanged. These route through `/invoice/payment-return`, which navigates only to fixed invoice destinations using the supplied invoice hash and status. It does not accept arbitrary redirect URLs or restore a client session. The destination applies the normal invoice access checks.

Use top-level browser navigation for the return flow, as the bundled PayPal adapter does.

Keep `notify_url` for server-to-server notifications. A successful browser return is not proof of payment; verify the provider callback and payment details before applying funds or marking the invoice paid.

## Testing

{% steps %}
1. Enable test mode and pay a test invoice. Confirm the record in **Invoicing → Transactions** and check that the invoice is paid.
2. Test an invalid webhook signature, an underpayment, and a currency mismatch through the payment paths your adapter supports. Verify that validation failures apply no credit.
3. Redeliver the same successful webhook and confirm there is only one credit for the payment. If your adapter also processes a browser callback, test both arrival orders and concurrent delivery.
4. Test browser returns for success and cancellation, including an expired browser session.
{% /steps %}

## Examples

See existing adapters in the [source code](https://github.com/FOSSBilling/FOSSBilling/tree/main/src/library/Payment/Adapter/) for real-world implementations like Stripe and PayPal.
